## Data Model

**Platform:** Microsoft Dataverse  
**Publisher Prefix:** `ac_`

### Table 1: Asset (`ac_asset`)

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Asset Name | Text (primary) | e.g. Dell Latitude 5450 |
| Asset Tag | Text, required | Unique key (`Unique Tag`), e.g. `LAP-001` |
| Type | Choice | Laptop, Monitor, Mouse, Keyboard |
| Condition | Choice | New, Good, Damaged, Under Repair |
| Status | Choice | Available, Checked Out, Maintenance |
| Serial Number | Text | Optional |
| Purchase Date | Date only | Optional |

### Table 2: Checkout (`ac_checkout`)

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Checkout Number | Text (primary) | Generated by the flow, e.g. `CO-20261017135401` |
| Asset | Lookup to Asset | Required |
| Assigned User | Lookup to User | Required |
| From | Date and time | Set when checked out |
| Due | Date and time | Required |
| Returned On | Date and time | Empty until returned |
| Checkout Status | Choice | Active, Returned |
| Reminder Sent | Yes/No | Prevents duplicate reminder emails |
| Notify Email | Email | Recipient of the reminder (if added) |

### Relationship

One Asset has many Checkouts (one-to-many, via the Asset lookup).

An asset can have many checkouts over time, but only one Active checkout at a time.

### Business Rules

- An asset can be checked out only when its Status is `Available`.
- Checkout and return are handled by Power Automate flows, not directly by the app.
- A reminder email is sent once when an active checkout is due within 24 hours.
- An overdue checkout is Active with a Due date earlier than the current date and time.
